[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪♪♪

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're having
a good time out there.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:17.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.379 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I think one
of the reasons, again,

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.650
people are happy to see you,
they're happy to hear you,

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.385
is you have this idea of,
"I'm going to give you

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
$1,000 a month
if I win this thing."

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:30.423
Now, obviously, Democrats
who are onstage with you -

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:33.793
a lot of them have big ideas for
healthcare, education.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.496
They think that your plan is
maybe going a little too far

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:40.667
So explain, really quickly, this
universal-basic-income idea.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, why you think it is
the core

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.939 line:92%
of what is behind your plan.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.407 line:92%
-First, it's not my idea at all.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been with United States
since our founding.

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:52.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thomas Paine was for it.
Martin Luther King was for it.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.848
And one state has had a dividend
for almost 40 years,

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
where everyone in Alaska
gets between

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.517 line:92%
$1,000 and $2,000 a year.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whoo!
-Whoo!

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.721 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Some Alaskans.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:04.557
And, so, what they're doin
for Alaska with oil money

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
we can do for everyone
in the country

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:06.826 size:81% position:41% line:92%
with technology money,

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.796
because right now, we're in th
midst of the greatest economic

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
transformation in
the history of our country

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's what got
Donald Trump elected.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
The fact we blasted away
4 million manufacturing jobs

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:19.372
in Michigan, Ohio, Pennsylvania,
Wisconsin, Iowa,

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
all the swing
states that he needed to win

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.877
So we need to take the bounty of
the 21st century economy

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:24.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
and start returning it
to people.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.514
And though everyone associates
me with 1,000 bucks a month,

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:29.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's really about what
the money would do for us.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:33.019
It's going to make us stronger
healthier, mentally healthier.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's going to improve
our relationships

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.288 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and our way of life.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You talk about how things -
-There isn't applause?

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:41.528 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:45.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They were all --
They were being quiet becaus

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were jealous of those
two Alaskans

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.302 line:92%
with the $1,000 in their pocket.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:49.769 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're like,
"They already got it."

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:56.276 size:81% position:41%
You talk about how GDP
and the stock market

00:02:56.276 --> 00:03:01.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
are bad indicators of exactl
where this country is at,

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.550 line:92%
as far as its economic health.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it may seem trite,
but you think that

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.955
we need to judge economic health
on happiness.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.891
Is that an accurate distillation
of the way you think?

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:14.761
-It's not quite happiness,
but that's essentially right

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where GDP's at record high
right now,

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:20.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
also at record highs -- stress
financial insecurity,

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
even suicides
and drug overdoses.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:25.838
It's gotten so bad that
even though our record high GDP,

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:29.275
our life expectancy has declined
for three years in a row.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.143 line:92%
The first time in 100 years.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.545
So you have to ask yourself,
are the measurements wrong

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:36.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
or are we actually prioritizin
this production number

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
over the life-span
of our people?

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.619 size:88% position:44%
And, to me, it's obvious
the numbers are wrong,

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you need to update the
to include things like

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
our health and well-being,
our mental health,

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:45.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
and freedom from
substance abuse,

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also things like clean air
and clean water,

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.095 line:92%
how our kids are doing --

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:52.031 size:78% position:39%
the real measurements
for American success.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:59.138
You talk about the numbers
